A||||8||sjp777||Over the roof scoop||||5||
Z||000000||sjp777||04-15-2001||11:43 AM||||I love those indy style scoops that come up over the top of the roof like Oreif has on his car. They look cool as all hell, but it's my understanding that they are non-functional. Is that the case? And does anyone know of anyone that makes a functional one?<P>I seem to remember IRM selling one  afew years back that attached to the passenger side deck vent and really flowed air.<P>Anybody got the "scoop" on these?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-15-2001||01:16 PM||||Mine came from IRM. Yes they state they are non-functional But all you need to do is cut out the opening and a hole in your decklid and then they are functional! Mine is used for cooling but you can hook it up and duct it to the engine also.<BR>The side ones called Fi-Air-O scoops are the ones that go above the roof. IRM doesn't sell them anymore. Not sure if someone else does. FOCOA has what is called Lazy C's. They wrap around the trailing edge if the notchback cars. I think they have a fan kit for them also.<P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Scoop_2.jpg">    <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||04-15-2001||08:37 PM||||Hey OreiF were u at Fierorama 2000 I think I might of seen your car there?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-16-2001||09:53 AM||||Yes, I was at Fierorama. I was parked under a tree across from Archie's. If you go to Archie's site or NIFE's site you can see the pics Archie took.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHarry||04-16-2001||11:46 PM||||Oreif, thats a nice job you did there. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Did you put a screen in the opening?<BR>I couldnt tell from the pics...<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||12
Z||000005||Oreif||04-16-2001||11:51 PM||||There is a stainless steel screen on the front of the scoop to keep bugs and debris out. I used the same screening on my side scoop too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroHarry||04-17-2001||12:03 AM||||Oreif,<BR>What kind of expanded metal did you use?<BR>I have looked everywhere and can find none to match the honey comb of the dash vents..<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||04-17-2001||12:21 AM||||It's not expanded metal. It is a stainless steel wire screen used on industrial air filters. The screen is very stiff. Think of it as the same screen used for house windows but about 3 times stiffer/thicker and made out of stainless steel.<BR>Since my car is black I wanted silver screening to accent it. If you want screening like the dash, just get a grate for a notchback and take the screen off the bottom. (same hex shape) Then paint it the color of your choice.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroHarry||04-17-2001||12:49 AM||||Thanks Ill look into that one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||10
